{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/378294-changeling-the-dreaming-can-do-will-kiths-change-over-time","id":378294,"title":"[Changeling: The Dreaming] Can/Do/Will Kiths change over time?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-22T12:52:10-08:00","id":378294,"title":"[Changeling: The Dreaming] Can/Do/Will Kiths change over time?","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">[The following is an open-ended discussion-prompt about the nature of CtD kiths. I\u2019m not looking for anything specific; just soliciting general opinions.]</span><br /> <br /> The Fae of old and the Kithian of today are different critters. To my understanding, modern Kithian \u2013 in addition to adopting the Changeling Way \u2013 enveloped themselves in the myths of yore; satyrs, trolls, redcaps, etc. for further protection against Banality.<br /> <br /> With many elements of the fantasy genre being less \u201cunderground\u201d now than in the mid-1990s (thanks to the popularity of <i>Lord of the Rings</i>, <i>World of Warcraft</i>, and the like), do you think Kiths could change over time? For example, could bygone myths of redcaps morph into contemporary and well-known critters, like WoW orcs or Urak-Hai?<br /> How does human culture impact Kiths, if at all?<br /> How organic and/or evolving do you think Kiths should be?<br /> Or shouldn\u2019t be?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T14:07:46-08:00","id":378376,"title":"","content":"It always seemed to me that the World of Darkness implies (well, also outright states) that old mythology has foundation in real supernaturals, the kind that are still around today. By that interpretation, it would be a mistake to say that because our cultural myths and stories have changed, that &quot;real&quot; fantastic creatures like the Fae will as well.<br /> <br /> In fact I think it's more likely that fiction within the World of Darkness will resemble its hidden reality more closely, and therefore turn out different from ours...or, that it'll be pushed in different directions by whatever shadowy illuminati splatbooks you prefer, and wind up even more completely different.<br /> <br /> Changeling in specific? Well...sure, let's take Redcaps for example. Do you suppose they want people to keep being afraid of them? Surely they'd like fiction to hint at what they're really like, so their legacy sticks with people even if they don't know it's real. Do they want to stay secretive? Then if they help nudge myths and stories and movies away from looking like them, it would be awfully silly for them to become like those same stories instead. This does imply a lot more control than any group really has, but I still think it's useful to think in that direction.<br /> <br /> Doesn't mean your friendly local Redcap wouldn't get a kick out of dressing up like Garrosh Hellscream to chase some WoW nerds with an axe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T05:36:07-08:00","id":378930,"title":"","content":"A Changeling evolving is unlikely, due to the fact that their mere existence flies in the face of the Consensus. However I would say that it is possible, due to the existence of the Inanimae known as the &quot;Kingdom of Flickers&quot;- more recent creations that are built off people's dreams when they view film.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T02:36:00-08:00","id":380869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sarah RPs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/378294-changeling-the-dreaming-can-do-will-kiths-change-over-time?p=378930#post378930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Changeling evolving is unlikely, due to the fact that their mere existence flies in the face of the Consensus. However I would say that it is possible, due to the existence of the Inanimae known as the &quot;Kingdom of Flickers&quot;- more recent creations that are built off people's dreams when they view film.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings do evolve, though it is unlikely it would happen within the current metaplot timeline. Sluagh are a great example of how they were formless shadows that evolved into what they are now, physically transforming and changing over hundreds of years. Will Kiths evolve? Yes. Will they evolve over a 20-50 year time frame? Unlikely. The &quot;Consensus&quot; is actually what makes them evolve, not themselves. It's the stories, the myths, the legends that are believed by the populace. As that changes, so to do the Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4579-skeleton-jack","name":"Skeleton Jack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}